  "story_id": "S099",
  "title": "V-ATPase, CAML, PI4KA, VPS, and DHDDs perturbations enter a shared endomembrane-proteostasis neighborhood with cell-specific inhibitory markers",
  "status": "grounded",
  "rejection_reason": null,
  "exact_observed_result": "Atp6v0c loss recurrently reduced Atp6v0a1 and had positive signature-neighbor links to proteasome, clathrin, Sec31a, Caml, Hspa9, Vps, and V-ATPase perturbations. Caml reproducibly induced Stmn4 in inhibitory classes; Pi4ka repressed Slc12a5 in 191 MB P MY GABA and exposed a low-n Abca2/Dgkd/Rap1gap pineal lead; Dhdds, Vps54, and Vps53 each sat near endomembrane, ER, V-ATPase, or proteasome neighbors with modest correlations.",
  "biological_interpretation": "The story is a convergence neighborhood rather than a single linear pathway: vesicle acidification, ER glycosylation/lipid synthesis, PI4P synthesis, CAML, and GARP/EARP perturbations repeatedly intersect endomembrane-proteostasis expression states, while individual marker genes remain cell-type-specific.",
